<BaseLayout lang="en" path="/en/about/" title="Anton Vladislavovich Nazarov (Antiokh) — Biography" description="Official biography of Anton Vladislavovich Nazarov, also known as Antiokh: IT manager, CTO, systems architect, and NeedleBit founder in Belgrade.">
  <section class="page-hero wrap"><span class="section-label">Biography / official profile</span><h1>Anton Vladislavovich Nazarov.<br /><em>An engineering manager outside the ivory tower.</em></h1></section>
  <section class="bio wrap"><aside><div class="bio-card"><span>At a glance</span><dl><dt>Full name</dt><dd>Anton Vladislavovich Nazarov</dd><dt>Handle</dt><dd>Antiokh</dd><dt>Location</dt><dd>Belgrade, Serbia</dd><dt>Languages</dt><dd>Russian · English · Serbian</dd><dt>Experience</dt><dd>18 years</dd></dl></div></aside><div class="prose"><p class="intro">I build and rebuild products and internal systems at the intersection of engineering, business, and operations.</p><h2>What that means</h2><p>Over 18 years, I have worked across startups, enterprise, banking, and government environments. I led the IT function of a 145-person cultural center, moved 100+ people to remote work, developed an industry system for a network of cultural institutions, and shipped client products from idea to production.</p><p>The recurring pattern is fragmented processes, weak tooling, and unclear ownership. I turn those conditions into systems teams can actually run and govern.</p><h2>The role I take</h2><p>I work as a playing coach: senior enough to align direction, architecture, and stakeholders; hands-on enough to build an integration, review SQL, prototype a workflow, or carry a release across the line.</p><h2>Not Mortimer</h2><p>Mortimer, the author associated with “Conscious Mercantilism,” has the same full name: Anton Vladislavovich Nazarov. We are different people. This is the official site of <strong>Antiokh</strong>, an IT manager and systems architect in Belgrade and the founder of NeedleBit.</p><h2>Education</h2><p>Bachelor’s degree in Management with a Small Business Management specialization, plus professional retraining in Information Technology Management. I also studied Applied Informatics in Economics and have a background in accounting and finance.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
